// The game's own help text, in English. A topic number is the one the screens' help areas name
// (`help_screens.ron`). A topic that is not here opens nothing.
[
    (index: 216, title: "Game", text: "Opens the save and load screen. From there you can also change the settings or leave the game. The shortcut is {key:game_menu}.", include: Some(900)),
    (index: 217, title: "Spells", text: "Opens your spell book, from which you cast overland spells. Spells for battle are cast in the battle itself. The shortcut is {key:spellbook}."),
    (index: 218, title: "Armies", text: "Lists all of your stacks of units. Pick one to centre the map on it, or open a unit's sheet. The shortcut is {key:army_list}."),
    (index: 219, title: "Cities", text: "Lists all of your cities with their size, what they are building and what they produce. Pick one to open it."),
    (index: 220, title: "Magic", text: "Opens your magic screen: how your power is split between mana, research and casting skill, what you are casting and researching, and the enchantments you keep up. The shortcut is {key:magic}."),
    (index: 221, title: "Information", text: "Opens the list of advisors: the Surveyor, Cartographer, Apprentice, Historian, Astrologer, Chancellor, Tax Collector, Grand Vizier and the Mirror. The shortcut is {key:advisors}."),
    (index: 222, title: "Plane", text: "Switches the map between Arcanus and Myrror. With units selected, the units change plane instead if they are standing where they can (a tower of wizardry, or a plane gate)."),
    (index: 223, title: "Done", text: "Cancels the orders of the selected units, such as a march in progress, so they stay where they are. The shortcut is {key:done}."),
    (index: 225, title: "Wait", text: "Puts the selected stack aside for now and selects the next stack that still has moves left. The stack comes back later in the turn. The shortcut is {key:wait}."),
    (index: 226, title: "Build", text: "The special action of the selected units: settlers found a city, engineers build a road, a unit that can purify cleanses corrupted land, and a spirit melds with a magic node. The shortcut is {key:special}."),
    (index: 229, title: "Next turn", text: "Ends your turn once no unit is left waiting for orders. The other wizards then play, and the next turn begins. The shortcut is {key:end_turn}."),
    (index: 231, title: "Gold", text: "The gold in your treasury. Gold pays for buildings and units you buy, and for upkeep."),
    (index: 232, title: "Mana", text: "The mana in your reserve. Mana pays for spells, for the upkeep of the spells you keep up, and for summoned creatures."),
    (index: 233, title: "Gold income", text: "The gold you gain or lose each turn: the taxes of your cities less the upkeep of buildings and units. If the treasury cannot pay, you are asked which units to let go before the turn ends."),
    (index: 234, title: "Food", text: "The food your cities produce each turn less what your units eat. If it is negative, you are asked which units to let go before the turn ends."),
    (index: 235, title: "Mana income", text: "The mana you gain or lose each turn: what your cities and nodes produce, less the upkeep of the spells you keep up. A negative figure drains your reserve; when the reserve runs out, you are asked which spells to give up."),
    (index: 236, title: "Moves", text: "How many moves the selected units have left this turn. A stack moves at the speed of its slowest unit."),
    (index: 900, title: "Keys", text: "Click a stack to select it, and right-click a square to send it there. {key:end_turn} ends the turn, {key:wait} waits, {key:done} cancels orders, {key:special} founds a city, builds a road, purifies or melds, {key:unselect} unselects.
Move the selected stack with {key:move_left}, {key:move_right}, {key:move_up} and {key:move_down}; the diagonals are {key:move_up_left}, {key:move_up_right}, {key:move_down_left} and {key:move_down_right}.
{key:scroll_left}, {key:scroll_right}, {key:scroll_up} and {key:scroll_down} scroll the map when nothing is selected, or with Shift held. Zoom in with {key:zoom_in} and out with {key:zoom_out}. {key:other_plane} shows the other plane and {key:centre} centres the map on the stack.
{key:magic} opens magic, {key:spellbook} your spells, {key:army_list} your armies, {key:advisors} the advisors and {key:game_menu} the game menu. The advisors have keys of their own: {key:surveyor} Surveyor, {key:cartographer} Cartographer, {key:apprentice} Apprentice, {key:history} Historian, {key:astrologer} Astrologer, {key:chancellor} Chancellor, {key:tax_collector} Tax Collector, {key:grand_vizier} Grand Vizier, {key:mirror} Mirror.
{key:quick_save} saves, {key:quick_load} loads, {key:undo} takes back your last move, {key:balance_farmers} balances the farmers and {key:console} opens the console.
To change a key, copy its line from hotkeys.ron into saves/hotkeys.ron."),
    (index: 214, title: "Page back", text: "Turns to the previous page of your spell book."),
    (index: 215, title: "Page forward", text: "Turns to the next page of your spell book."),
    (index: 0, title: "Close spell book", text: "Closes the spell book without casting anything."),
    (index: 224, title: "Patrol", text: "Sets the units of the selected stack aside: they are not asked for orders again until you move them. Unlike Done, which only skips them for this turn."),
    (index: 237, title: "Map", text: "Shows where the selected unit stands on its plane. The blinking white dot is the unit."),
    (index: 238, title: "Unit name", text: "The name or type of the highlighted unit."),
    (index: 239, title: "Unit enchantments", text: "The enchantments on the highlighted unit."),
    (index: 240, title: "Items", text: "Opens the item screen, where you give magic items to your heroes."),
    (index: 242, title: "Upkeep", text: "What your armies cost you each turn in food, gold and mana."),
    (index: 243, title: "Empty hero slot", text: "A hero you hire appears here."),
    (index: 244, title: "Scroll up", text: "Scrolls the list up one row."),
    (index: 245, title: "Scroll down", text: "Scrolls the list down one row."),
    (index: 246, title: "Anvil", text: "Destroys the magic item you hold, giving you half its value in mana."),
    (index: 247, title: "Alchemy", text: "Converts gold to mana or mana to gold. With the Alchemy retort you get one for one; without it, two for one."),
    (index: 249, title: "Map", text: "Shows where the highlighted city stands on its plane. The blinking white dot is the city."),
    (index: 250, title: "City name", text: "The name of the highlighted city."),
    (index: 251, title: "City enchantments", text: "The enchantments on the highlighted city."),
    (index: 265, title: "Casting skill", text: "Your casting skill: how much mana you can put into spells in one turn. The slider puts more of your power into it."),
    (index: 266, title: "Mana", text: "The share of your power that goes into your mana reserve. Spells you keep up are paid from the reserve. If you put in less than you spend, the reserve runs out, and you are asked which enchantments and creatures to give up."),
    (index: 267, title: "Research", text: "The share of your power that goes into research. Each point adds a research point to the spell you are researching, on top of the points your libraries, sage guilds and other buildings give."),
    (index: 270, title: "Enchantments", text: "The overland enchantments now in force. The colour of a spell is the colour of the wizard who cast it."),
    (index: 271, title: "Relations", text: "How the wizard in the gem feels about you: hate, troubled, tense, restless, unease, neutral, relaxed, calm, peaceful, friendly or harmony."),
    (index: 273, title: "Casting skill", text: "How much mana you can put into spells in one turn. The first number is your casting skill plus the help of heroes standing on your fortress (half their mana each); the number in brackets is your own skill."),
    (index: 276, title: "Casting", text: "The spell you are casting now."),
    (index: 293, title: "City name", text: "The name and size of the city."),
    (index: 295, title: "Food", text: "What the city's farms and fishing grounds produce. Each farmer makes food according to the city's race. The icons on the left are the food the city's people eat, and those on the right the surplus, which feeds your units. A grey icon means the city is short of food and starving. A large icon is 10 food, a small one 1."),
    (index: 296, title: "Production", text: "What the city makes each turn toward its buildings and units. Workers produce according to their race. A large icon is 10 production, a small one 1."),
    (index: 297, title: "Gold", text: "On the left, what the city costs you each turn in upkeep; on the right, its net income after upkeep. Rivers, oceans, marketplaces, banks and merchants guilds raise it. A large icon is 10 gold, a small one 1."),
    (index: 299, title: "Magical power", text: "The power the city adds to your income. Some races make power by nature, and so do shrines, temples, parthenons, libraries and other buildings. A large icon is 10 power, a small one 1."),
    (index: 300, title: "Spell research", text: "The research the city adds each turn to the spell you are researching, from its buildings. A large icon is 10 research, a small one 1."),
    (index: 301, title: "Enchantments", text: "The enchantments on the city, in the colour of the wizard who cast each."),
    (index: 302, title: "City view", text: "The city and the land around it. The city works the lit squares and not the darkened corners. A square that a neighbouring city also works gives each city half its value."),
    (index: 303, title: "Cityscape", text: "The city's buildings. Point at a building to see its name, and click it to sell it."),
    (index: 304, title: "Producing", text: "What the city is building and how many turns are left."),
    (index: 305, title: "Buy", text: "Buys what the city is building for gold, finishing it by the next turn. It needs enough gold."),
    (index: 306, title: "Change", text: "Chooses what the city builds."),
    (index: 776, title: "Population", text: "The city's population, with the growth per turn in brackets. Each townsfolk figure is a thousand people."),
    (index: 350, title: "Portrait", text: "The wizard's portrait, in a gem of the wizard's banner colour."),
    (index: 351, title: "Name", text: "The wizard's name."),
    (index: 353, title: "Gold", text: "The gold in the wizard's treasury."),
    (index: 354, title: "Mana", text: "The mana in the wizard's reserve, which pays for spells."),
    (index: 355, title: "Spell ranks", text: "The wizard's books in each realm of magic. One book is one spell pick."),
    (index: 357, title: "Heroes", text: "The heroes who serve the wizard."),
    (index: 358, title: "Plane", text: "The name of the plane on show."),
    (index: 359, title: "Map", text: "Everything you have explored of this plane, reduced. Cities are squares, and units are dots in their owner's colour. Click a point to centre the main map on it."),
    (index: 360, title: "Close", text: "Closes the map."),
    (index: 361, title: "Change planes", text: "Click the fold to switch between Arcanus and Myrror."),
    (index: 362, title: "Map key", text: "The wizards you have met and their colours."),
    (index: 363, title: "Power graph", text: "Each wizard's overall power, turn by turn."),
    (index: 364, title: "Status", text: "Compares the wizards in several areas. The longer the bar, the stronger the wizard."),
    (index: 382, title: "Moves", text: "How many moves the unit has in a turn."),
    (index: 496, title: "Upkeep", text: "What the unit costs you each turn in gold, food and mana."),
    (index: 383, title: "Melee", text: "The unit's strength in hand to hand fighting, one icon for each point. A gold icon is a bonus from a spell or ability, a darkened icon a penalty."),
    (index: 387, title: "Ranged attack", text: "The unit's strength with a missile, thrown or magic attack, one icon for each point. A gold icon is a bonus from a spell or ability, a darkened icon a penalty."),
    (index: 393, title: "Defence", text: "The unit's armour, one icon for each point. A gold icon is a bonus from a spell or ability, a darkened icon a penalty."),
    (index: 394, title: "Resistance", text: "The unit's resistance to spells, one icon for each point. A gold icon is a bonus from a spell or ability, a darkened icon a penalty."),
    (index: 395, title: "Hits", text: "The unit's hit points, one icon for each. A gold icon is a bonus from a spell or ability, a darkened icon damage the unit has taken."),
    (index: 497, title: "Page up", text: "Scrolls the list up one page."),
    (index: 498, title: "Page down", text: "Scrolls the list down one page."),
    (index: 499, title: "Dismiss", text: "Gets rid of a unit you no longer need."),
    (index: 501, title: "Cityscape", text: "The city's buildings. Point at a building to see its name."),
    (index: 502, title: "Garrison", text: "The troops in the city."),
    (index: 507, title: "Outpost", text: "The outpost as it looks now."),
    (index: 628, title: "Continue", text: "Loads and plays on from the game you played last."),
    (index: 629, title: "Load game", text: "Opens the saved games, where you can load one or change the settings."),
    (index: 630, title: "New game", text: "Starts a new game."),
    (index: 631, title: "Quit", text: "Leaves the game."),
    (index: 633, title: "Load / OK", text: "On the load screen, loads the selected game. On the settings screen, accepts the settings and closes it."),
    (index: 634, title: "Back", text: "Goes back to the main menu."),
    (index: 635, title: "Settings", text: "Opens the settings, where you can change how the game looks, sounds and plays."),
    (index: 638, title: "Saved games", text: "Click a game to select it, and Load to play it."),
    (index: 642, title: "Difficulty", text: "How well the computer wizards play, and how much help they get: Intro, Easy, Average, Hard or Impossible."),
    (index: 648, title: "Opponents", text: "How many computer wizards you face, from one to four. They play on both planes."),
    (index: 649, title: "Land size", text: "How much of each plane is land: the number and size of the continents."),
    (index: 653, title: "Magic power", text: "How strong the magic nodes are. A Myrror node makes twice what an Arcanus node does."),
    (index: 675, title: "Sound effects", text: "Switches the sound effects on or off."),
    (index: 676, title: "Background music", text: "Switches the music that plays during the game on or off."),
    (index: 677, title: "Event music", text: "Switches the special music for events and reports on or off."),
    (index: 678, title: "City spell events", text: "Whether you see spells with a lasting effect on a city, yours or an enemy's, being cast."),
    (index: 679, title: "Overland spell events", text: "Whether you see overland enchantments, yours or an enemy's, being cast."),
    (index: 680, title: "Summoning events", text: "Whether you see a creature or hero being summoned."),
    (index: 681, title: "End of turn summary", text: "Whether the summary of your turn is shown when the turn ends."),
    (index: 683, title: "Random events", text: "Whether random events, good or bad, happen to you and to the other wizards."),
    (index: 684, title: "End of turn wait", text: "On: when every unit has been given its orders, you press Next Turn to end the turn. Off: the turn ends by itself as soon as the last unit has been given its orders."),
    (index: 685, title: "Strategic combat only", text: "When on, every battle you start is fought by the battle AI without opening the battle screen. You are asked how much mana it may spend, and then see the result. When off, you choose for each battle between fighting it yourself and the Auto button."),
    (index: 686, title: "Auto unit information", text: "Whether pointing at a unit in battle shows its attack, moves left, defence, resistance, ammunition, mana, level and hit points."),
    (index: 687, title: "Enemy moves", text: "Whether the map follows the enemy troops you can see while they move."),
    (index: 688, title: "Enemy spells", text: "Whether you see the spells that enemy wizards cast."),
    (index: 690, title: "Spell animations", text: "Whether the pictures that play when you cast a spell are shown."),
    (index: 692, title: "Expanding help", text: "Whether a help box grows out from the place you pointed at."),
    (index: 806, title: "Raze city", text: "Whether you are asked if you want to raze a city after conquering it. When off, you can still raze a captured city by pressing R while the battle results are on the screen."),
    // Abilities and spells are opened by the `help` index of their row in abilities.ron and spells.ron, not by a screen area.
    (index: 1000, title: "Armour Piercing", text: "Halves the defence of the target before it blocks. Shields and armour count for half against this unit's blows."),
    (index: 1001, title: "Asleep", text: "The unit cannot move, attack or fly. Every blow against it does full damage because it cannot defend itself."),
    (index: 1002, title: "Bow", text: "A ranged attack with arrows. Each figure shoots once, using up one arrow. Missile Immunity stops it."),
    (index: 1003, title: "Doom Bolt Spell", text: "The unit can cast Doom Bolt once in a battle, for no mana: 10 points of damage that ignore defence."),
    (index: 1004, title: "Fireball Spell", text: "The unit can cast Fireball once in a battle, for no mana: an explosion that hits every figure of the target unit."),
    (index: 1005, title: "Healing Spell", text: "The unit can cast Healing once in a battle, for no mana: it heals a friendly unit by 5 hit points."),
    (index: 1006, title: "Web Spell", text: "The unit can cast Web once in a battle, for no mana: the target unit is held in a web until it breaks free."),
    (index: 1007, title: "Cause Fear", text: "Each figure of an enemy unit in melee with this unit must pass a death resistance check, or it cannot strike. Death Immunity and Magic Immunity are not afraid."),
    (index: 1008, title: "Cavalry", text: "Mounted troops, fast on open ground."),
    (index: 1009, title: "Cold Immunity", text: "Cold attacks (ice bolts, ice storms) do nothing to this unit."),
    (index: 1010, title: "Confused", text: "A confused unit cannot be trusted. Each turn it either stands about, wanders to a random square, is led by the enemy, or acts as usual."),
    (index: 1011, title: "Create Outpost", text: "This unit can found a new city on the square where it stands, using up its move. The unit is spent in the founding."),
    (index: 1012, title: "Create Undead", text: "Units killed by this unit rise again as undead on its side."),
    (index: 1013, title: "Death Bolt", text: "A ranged attack with a bolt of death magic. Resistance of the target counts against it."),
    (index: 1014, title: "Death Gaze", text: "A gaze that kills. A target that fails a resistance check dies; Death Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 1015, title: "Death Immunity", text: "Spells that kill, frighten or drain life do nothing to this unit."),
    (index: 1016, title: "Dispel Evil", text: "Banishes evil creatures: undead and creatures of chaos and death take heavy damage from this unit's attack unless they resist."),
    (index: 1017, title: "Drow Bolt", text: "A ranged attack with a bolt of dark magic. The target's resistance counts against it."),
    (index: 1018, title: "Eldritch Weapon", text: "The unit's attacks are magical, and the defender blocks with one point less defence."),
    (index: 1019, title: "Fire Breath", text: "A ranged breath of flame. Fire Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 1020, title: "Fire Immunity", text: "Fire attacks (fire breath, fire spells) do nothing to this unit."),
    (index: 1021, title: "Fireball", text: "A ranged attack with a ball of fire that burns the target. Fire Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 1022, title: "First Strike", text: "The unit strikes before the defender can answer in melee. Negate First Strike cancels it."),
    (index: 1023, title: "Flying", text: "The unit flies, so it crosses any terrain, water included, for one move a square. Units on foot strike a flier at half strength in melee."),
    (index: 1024, title: "Forester", text: "The unit crosses forests at the cost of one move a square instead of two. A unit that has this ability gives it to every unit in its stack. It helps units that have two or more moves; a unit with a single move can enter a forest whatever its cost."),
    (index: 1025, title: "Haste", text: "The unit moves twice as far and attacks, or shoots, twice a turn."),
    (index: 1026, title: "Healer", text: "Heals every other unit of its stack by an extra 20% of its hit points at the start of each turn."),
    (index: 1027, title: "Holy Bonus", text: "Strengthened by holy magic: the unit and its side gain extra attack, defence and resistance, and its attack harms evil creatures more."),
    (index: 1028, title: "Ice Bolt", text: "A ranged attack with a bolt of ice. Cold Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 1029, title: "Illusion", text: "An illusion that ignores the defence of its target. Only units that can see through illusions block normally."),
    (index: 1030, title: "Illusion Immunity", text: "The unit sees through illusions, so illusion attacks do not ignore its defence."),
    (index: 1031, title: "Immolation", text: "Flames burn the units that attack this unit in melee, hurting them as they strike."),
    (index: 1032, title: "Invisibility", text: "Enemies that cannot see through illusions are at -1 to hit the unit, in melee and at range."),
    (index: 1033, title: "Large Shield", text: "A large shield gives extra defence against missile attacks (arrows, slings and thrown weapons)."),
    (index: 1034, title: "Life Steal", text: "The unit drains life from its victims; they can resist it."),
    (index: 1035, title: "Lightning Bolt", text: "A ranged attack with a lightning bolt that pierces armour. Magic Immunity protects against it."),
    (index: 1036, title: "Lightning Breath", text: "A ranged breath of lightning that pierces armour. Magic Immunity protects against it."),
    (index: 1037, title: "Long Range", text: "The unit's ranged attacks reach farther: it can shoot at targets far across the battlefield without losing strength."),
    (index: 1038, title: "Lucky", text: "Fortune favours this unit: it hits more often and its defence holds more often."),
    (index: 1039, title: "Magic Immunity", text: "Spells and magical ranged attacks do nothing to this unit, and it resists magic with +30."),
    (index: 1040, title: "Magical Weapon", text: "The unit's normal attacks count as magical, so Weapon Immunity does not stop them."),
    (index: 1041, title: "Meld", text: "The unit can merge with a magic node, and then it lives there and guards it."),
    (index: 1042, title: "Merging", text: "In a battle the unit moves instantly through the ground to any free square, for the cost of one move."),
    (index: 1043, title: "Missile Immunity", text: "Arrows, slings and thrown weapons do nothing to this unit."),
    (index: 1044, title: "Mountaineer", text: "The unit crosses mountains and hills at the cost of one move a square instead of three or two. A unit that has this ability gives it to every unit in its stack. It helps units that have two or more moves."),
    (index: 1045, title: "Multiple Gaze", text: "Several gazes in one attack, each of which the target must resist."),
    (index: 1046, title: "Nature Bolt", text: "A ranged attack with a bolt of nature magic. The target's resistance counts against it."),
    (index: 1047, title: "Negate First Strike", text: "Cancels the first strike of the enemy, so both sides strike together."),
    (index: 1048, title: "Non-Corporeal", text: "The unit has no body. It crosses any land for half a move and passes through walls, and Entangle cannot hold it."),
    (index: 1049, title: "Path Finding", text: "The unit and every unit stacked with it cross any land square for half a move, as if on a road."),
    (index: 1050, title: "Planar Travel", text: "The unit can shift between Arcanus and Myrror from any square with the Plane button, without a tower of power."),
    (index: 1051, title: "Poison Immunity", text: "The unit is not harmed by poison."),
    (index: 1052, title: "Poison Touch", text: "The unit's blows poison what they hit. A target that fails a resistance check suffers extra damage."),
    (index: 1053, title: "Purify", text: "The unit cleanses corrupted land."),
    (index: 1054, title: "Regeneration", text: "The unit heals fully at the start of each turn."),
    (index: 1055, title: "Resist All", text: "The unit resists every kind of elemental magic."),
    (index: 1056, title: "Rock Throwing", text: "A ranged attack by throwing rocks. Missile Immunity does not stop it."),
    (index: 1057, title: "Shaman Bolt", text: "A ranged attack with a bolt of shaman magic. The target's resistance counts against it."),
    (index: 1058, title: "Sling", text: "A ranged attack with a sling. Each figure shoots once, using up one stone. Missile Immunity stops it."),
    (index: 1059, title: "Sorcery Bolt", text: "A ranged attack with a bolt of sorcery. The target's resistance counts against it."),
    (index: 1060, title: "Spell Caster", text: "The unit casts spells in battle, paying from its own mana."),
    (index: 1061, title: "Major Spell Caster", text: "The unit casts spells in battle, paying from its own mana, which it has more of than an ordinary spellcaster."),
    (index: 1062, title: "Sprite Bolt", text: "A ranged attack with a bolt of pixie magic. The target's resistance counts against it."),
    (index: 1063, title: "Stoning Gaze", text: "A gaze that turns the target to stone. A figure that fails a resistance check dies. Stoning Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 1064, title: "Stoning Immunity", text: "The unit cannot be turned to stone."),
    (index: 1065, title: "Stoning Touch", text: "Figures hit by this unit's blows may be turned to stone if they fail a resistance check. Stoning Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 1066, title: "Creature Summoning", text: "The unit can summon demons in battle to fight beside it."),
    (index: 1067, title: "Teleport", text: "In a battle the unit moves to any free square, for the cost of one move."),
    (index: 1068, title: "Thrown", text: "A ranged attack with thrown weapons, used up one at a time. Missile Immunity stops it."),
    (index: 1069, title: "Wall Crusher", text: "Can breach city walls when it attacks a city: a melee blow destroys a wall section half the time, a ranged attack a quarter of the time."),
    (index: 1070, title: "Water Walking", text: "The unit walks on water as on land, without a ship. A unit that has this ability carries only itself."),
    (index: 1071, title: "Weapon Immunity", text: "Normal weapons barely hurt the unit: its defence is at least 10 against them, and normal arrows and thrown weapons are cut to the same. Heroes, fantastic creatures, magical weapons and spells ignore it."),
    (index: 1072, title: "Webbed", text: "The unit is held where it stands, and cannot fly, until the web is dispelled or the battle ends."),
    (index: 1073, title: "Wind Walking", text: "The unit carries every unit of its stack through the air, so the whole stack moves as if flying."),
    (index: 1074, title: "Leadership", text: "Raises the melee attack of the friendly normal units fighting beside the hero, and half as much their ranged attack. It grows with the hero's level; only the best leader on the field counts."),
    (index: 1075, title: "Super Leadership", text: "Superior Leadership: a larger bonus to the melee and ranged attack of the friendly normal units in battle. It grows with the hero's level; only the best leader on the field counts."),
    (index: 1076, title: "Legendary", text: "The hero's deeds add to the wizard's fame, more with every level."),
    (index: 1077, title: "Super Legendary", text: "Superior Legendary: the hero adds still more to the wizard's fame with every level."),
    (index: 1078, title: "Blademaster", text: "The hero hits more often, more so with every level."),
    (index: 1079, title: "Super Blademaster", text: "Superior Blademaster: the hero hits much more often, more so with every level."),
    (index: 1080, title: "Armsmaster", text: "At the end of each turn the other units on the hero's square gain experience, more with every level. Only the best Armsmaster counts."),
    (index: 1081, title: "Super Armsmaster", text: "Superior Armsmaster: the other units on the hero's square gain more experience each turn. Only the best Armsmaster counts."),
    (index: 1082, title: "Constitution", text: "The hero has more hit points, more with every level."),
    (index: 1083, title: "Super Constitution", text: "Superior Constitution: the hero has many more hit points, more with every level."),
    (index: 1084, title: "Might", text: "The hero's melee attack is higher, more so with every level."),
    (index: 1085, title: "Super Might", text: "Superior Might: the hero's melee attack is much higher, more so with every level."),
    (index: 1086, title: "Arcane Power", text: "A hero with a magic ranged attack strikes harder with it, more so with every level."),
    (index: 1087, title: "Super Arcane Power", text: "Superior Arcane Power: a hero with a magic ranged attack strikes much harder with it, more so with every level."),
    (index: 1088, title: "Sage", text: "The wizard's spell research goes faster, more so with every level of the hero."),
    (index: 1089, title: "Super Sage", text: "Superior Sage: the wizard's spell research goes much faster, more so with every level of the hero."),
    (index: 1090, title: "Prayermaster", text: "Adds to the resistance of all friendly units in battle, more with every level. The better of this and Resistance to All counts."),
    (index: 1091, title: "Super Prayermaster", text: "Superior Prayermaster: a larger bonus to the resistance of all friendly units in battle. The better of this and Resistance to All counts."),
    (index: 1092, title: "Agility", text: "The hero's defence is higher, more so with every level."),
    (index: 1093, title: "Super Agility", text: "Superior Agility: the hero's defence is much higher, more so with every level."),
    (index: 1094, title: "Charmed", text: "The hero never fails a resistance roll."),
    (index: 1095, title: "Noble", text: "The hero costs no upkeep and brings in 10 gold."),
    (index: 1096, title: "Female", text: "The hero is a woman."),
    (index: 1097, title: "Chaos Channeled", text: "Chaos Channels has changed this unit."),
    (index: 1098, title: "Death Touch", text: "A touch that makes the target resist or lose a figure. An item or a spell can give it."),
    (index: 1099, title: "Destruction", text: "An attack that makes the target resist or lose a figure outright. An item can give it."),
    (index: 1100, title: "Doom Damage", text: "The attack ignores defence: its strength is the damage. A unit that is given it by an item or a spell does half as much."),
    (index: 1101, title: "Land Corruption", text: "The unit's presence corrupts the land it stands on."),
    (index: 1102, title: "Power Drain", text: "The attack drains the mana of a spell caster."),
    (index: 1103, title: "Demon Skin", text: "Chaos Channels has given this unit demon-skin armour."),
    (index: 1104, title: "Demon Wings", text: "Chaos Channels has given this unit wings."),
    (index: 1105, title: "Demon Breath", text: "Chaos Channels has given this unit fire breath."),
    (index: 2000, title: "Earth to Mud", text: "Turns a square of the battlefield to mud, which slows the units that enter it."),
    (index: 2001, title: "Resist Elements", text: "Gives a unit +3 resistance, and +6 against fire, cold, lightning and nature magic, for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2002, title: "Wall of Stone", text: "Builds city walls in one of your cities that has none."),
    (index: 2003, title: "Giant Strength", text: "Adds +1 to a unit's melee attack for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2004, title: "Web", text: "Entangles an enemy unit in a web. It cannot move, attack or fly until the web is dispelled."),
    (index: 2005, title: "War Bears", text: "Summons War Bears onto the chosen square: melee 7, defence 3, resistance 6, 2 figures of 8 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Forester."),
    (index: 2006, title: "Stone Skin", text: "Adds +1 to a unit's defence for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2007, title: "Water Walking", text: "Lets a unit walk on water as on land for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2008, title: "Sprites", text: "Summons Sprites onto the chosen square: melee 2, ranged 3, defence 2, resistance 8, 4 figures of 1 hit point, 2 moves. Abilities: Flying, Forester, Sprite Bolt."),
    (index: 2009, title: "Earth Lore", text: "Reveals the terrain and the features of the squares round the target square on the map."),
    (index: 2010, title: "Cracks Call", text: "Opens a fissure on the chosen square of the battlefield. A walking unit on that square falls in and dies one time in four; fliers and bodiless units are safe. A wall section on the square is destroyed."),
    (index: 2011, title: "Nature's Eye", text: "Gives the city a sight range of nine squares for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2012, title: "Ice Bolt", text: "A bolt of ice strikes one enemy unit. Each extra mana adds a point of strength. Cold Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 2013, title: "Giant Spiders", text: "Summons Giant Spiders onto the chosen square: melee 4, defence 3, resistance 7, 2 figures of 10 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Web Spell, Poison Touch."),
    (index: 2014, title: "Change Terrain", text: "Turns the chosen square into a different kind of land: mountains become hills, hills become plains, forests become plains, and so on up the scale."),
    (index: 2015, title: "Path Finding", text: "The unit and every unit in its stack cross any land square for half a move while the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2016, title: "Cockatrices", text: "Summons Cockatrices onto the chosen square: melee 4, defence 3, resistance 7, 4 figures of 3 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Flying, Stoning Touch."),
    (index: 2017, title: "Transmute", text: "Turns the metal of a mine or a mineral on the chosen square into a different one."),
    (index: 2018, title: "Nature's Cures", text: "Heals your units on the chosen square."),
    (index: 2019, title: "Basilisk", text: "Summons Basilisk onto the chosen square: melee 15, ranged 1, defence 4, resistance 7, 1 figure of 30 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Stoning Gaze."),
    (index: 2020, title: "Elemental Armor", text: "Gives a unit +10 defence against the elemental attacks of fire, cold, lightning and nature while the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2021, title: "Petrify", text: "Turns one unit to stone unless it resists. Stoning Immunity protects against it."),
    (index: 2022, title: "Stone Giant", text: "Summons Stone Giant onto the chosen square: melee 15, ranged 15, defence 8, resistance 9, 1 figure of 20 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Stoning Immunity, Poison Immunity, Wall Crusher, Mountaineer, Rock Throwing."),
    (index: 2023, title: "Iron Skin", text: "Adds +5 to a unit's defence for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2024, title: "Ice Storm", text: "A storm of ice strikes every unit on the chosen square. Units with Cold Immunity or Magic Immunity are not harmed."),
    (index: 2025, title: "Earthquake", text: "Shakes an enemy city. Each building has a 15% chance to be destroyed, and each non-flying corporeal unit in it a 25% chance to die."),
    (index: 2026, title: "Gorgons", text: "Summons Gorgons onto the chosen square: melee 8, ranged 1, defence 7, resistance 9, 4 figures of 9 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Flying, Stoning Gaze."),
    (index: 2027, title: "Move Fortress", text: "Moves your wizard's fortress to another of your cities on the same plane."),
    (index: 2028, title: "Gaia's Blessing", text: "Blesses the land round the city. A forest gives twice its production bonus (+6%), and the terrain gives 50% more food, which raises the most people the city can feed. Each turn every desert square has a 10% chance to turn to grassland, every volcano 10% to turn to hills, and every corrupted square 20% to come clean. Outposts grow faster and two rebels are pacified."),
    (index: 2029, title: "Earth Elemental", text: "Summons Earth Elemental to fight for you in the battle: melee 25, defence 4, resistance 8, 1 figure of 30 hit points, 1 move. Abilities: Stoning Immunity, Poison Immunity, Wall Crusher."),
    (index: 2030, title: "Regeneration", text: "Gives a unit the Regeneration ability for as long as the spell is kept up: it heals fully every turn."),
    (index: 2031, title: "Behemoth", text: "Summons Behemoth onto the chosen square: melee 25, defence 9, resistance 10, 1 figure of 45 hit points, 2 moves."),
    (index: 2032, title: "Entangle", text: "Vines hold the enemy: each enemy unit that walks and has a body loses one whole move at the start of its turn."),
    (index: 2033, title: "Nature Awareness", text: "Shows you the whole of both planes, for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2034, title: "Call Lightning", text: "At the start of each turn three to five bolts of strength 8 strike random enemy units. They pierce armour, and Magic Immunity stops them."),
    (index: 2035, title: "Colossus", text: "Summons Colossus onto the chosen square: melee 20, ranged 20, defence 10, resistance 15, 1 figure of 30 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Stoning Immunity, Poison Immunity, Wall Crusher, First Strike, Rock Throwing."),
    (index: 2036, title: "Earth Gate", text: "Makes the city an Earth Gate. A stack in it can step through to any other Earth Gate city of yours on the same plane, for one move."),
    (index: 2037, title: "Herb Mastery", text: "Your units that are not creatures of death heal each turn, wherever they are."),
    (index: 2038, title: "Great Wyrm", text: "Summons Great Wyrm onto the chosen square: melee 25, defence 12, resistance 12, 1 figure of 45 hit points, 3 moves. Abilities: Poison Touch, Merging."),
    (index: 2039, title: "Nature's Wrath", text: "While you keep it, any other wizard who casts a death or chaos spell on the map has the cities shaken: 10% of the non-flying corporeal units and 5% of the buildings in them are destroyed."),
    (index: 2040, title: "Resist Magic", text: "Gives a unit +5 resistance for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2041, title: "Dispel Magic True", text: "Like Dispel Magic, with three times the strength for the mana put in."),
    (index: 2042, title: "Floating Island", text: "Raises a floating island of land on the chosen square of ocean or water; units can stand on it."),
    (index: 2043, title: "Guardian Wind", text: "Gives a unit Missile Immunity for as long as the spell is kept up: arrows and slings do nothing to it."),
    (index: 2044, title: "Phantom Warriors", text: "Summons Phantom Warriors to fight for you in the battle: melee 3, defence 0, resistance 6, 6 figures of 1 hit point, 1 move. Abilities: Stoning Immunity, Death Immunity, Poison Immunity, Non-Corporeal, Illusion."),
    (index: 2045, title: "Confusion", text: "Confuses one enemy unit. Each turn it may stand about, wander off, be led by you or act as it likes."),
    (index: 2046, title: "Word of Recall", text: "Teleports one of your units from the battle to your wizard's fortress or summoning circle. The unit leaves the battle at once."),
    (index: 2047, title: "Counter Magic", text: "The mana you put in tries to stop every spell the enemy wizard casts in this battle. Each attempt drains five mana from the reserve, whether it works or not."),
    (index: 2048, title: "Nagas", text: "Summons Nagas onto the chosen square: melee 4, defence 3, resistance 7, 2 figures of 6 hit points, 1 move. Abilities: First Strike, Poison Touch."),
    (index: 2049, title: "Psionic Blast", text: "A mental blast strikes one enemy unit. Each two extra mana add a point of strength. Illusion Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 2050, title: "Blur", text: "Each point of damage an enemy attack deals to your units has a one in ten chance to miss, unless the attacker sees through illusions."),
    (index: 2051, title: "Disenchant True", text: "Removes enchantments of other wizards from a square of the map and everything on it, with a strength of 150."),
    (index: 2052, title: "Vertigo", text: "Dizzies one enemy unit: -2 to hit and -1 defence, unless it resists."),
    (index: 2053, title: "Spell Lock", text: "Makes a unit proof against dispelling: every enchantment on it is harder to remove while the spell lasts."),
    (index: 2054, title: "Enchant Road", text: "Enchants the roads on a square of the map. Units move along enchanted roads without using up any moves."),
    (index: 2055, title: "Flight", text: "Gives a unit Flying for as long as the spell is kept up. The unit gets at least three moves."),
    (index: 2056, title: "Wind Mastery", text: "Your ships and fliers move one and a half times as far. Every wizard without the spell moves them at half speed while anyone keeps it."),
    (index: 2057, title: "Spell Blast", text: "Blasts the spell an enemy wizard is casting: that casting is lost. It costs you as much mana as the wizard had put into it."),
    (index: 2058, title: "Aura of Majesty", text: "Wins the other wizards' goodwill: their attitude to you improves by 10 when you cast it and by 1 more each turn."),
    (index: 2059, title: "Phantom Beast", text: "Summons Phantom Beast to fight for you in the battle: melee 18, defence 0, resistance 8, 1 figure of 20 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Stoning Immunity, Death Immunity, Poison Immunity, Non-Corporeal, Illusion."),
    (index: 2060, title: "Disjunction True", text: "Destroys one overland enchantment of any wizard, for good, unless it resists. The spell is strong, so few enchantments resist it."),
    (index: 2061, title: "Invisibility", text: "Gives a unit Invisibility for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2062, title: "Wind Walking", text: "Gives a unit Wind Walking: it carries its whole stack through the air, and the unit gets at least 3 moves, for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2063, title: "Banish", text: "Banishes one fantastic creature unless it passes a resistance check at -3. Each 15 extra mana lowers its resistance by one more."),
    (index: 2064, title: "Storm Giant", text: "Summons Storm Giant onto the chosen square: melee 12, ranged 10, defence 7, resistance 9, 1 figure of 20 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Wall Crusher, Armour Piercing, Lightning Bolt."),
    (index: 2065, title: "Air Elemental", text: "Summons Air Elemental to fight for you in the battle: melee 15, defence 8, resistance 9, 1 figure of 10 hit points, 5 moves. Abilities: Stoning Immunity, Poison Immunity, Weapon Immunity, Flying, Invisibility."),
    (index: 2066, title: "Mind Storm", text: "Reduces melee, ranged attack, defence and resistance of one enemy unit by 5 each, with no check. Units that see through illusions are not harmed."),
    (index: 2067, title: "Stasis", text: "Freezes every enemy unit on the chosen square. A frozen unit has a chance to break free each turn, resisting at -5 against sorcery."),
    (index: 2068, title: "Magic Immunity", text: "Gives a unit Magic Immunity for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2069, title: "Haste", text: "Doubles a unit's moves in a battle and lets it attack, or shoot, twice a turn."),
    (index: 2070, title: "Djinn", text: "Summons Djinn onto the chosen square: melee 15, ranged 8, defence 8, resistance 10, 1 figure of 20 hit points, 3 moves. Abilities: Flying, Spell Caster, Wind Walking, Teleport, Ice Bolt."),
    (index: 2071, title: "Spell Ward", text: "Wards your city against one realm of magic, chosen when you cast it. Spells of that realm cannot be cast on the city or the units in it, its fantastic creatures cannot enter, and an attacker cannot cast them in a battle there. Each ward costs the upkeep."),
    (index: 2072, title: "Creature Binding", text: "Takes control of an enemy fantastic creature for the rest of the battle unless it resists."),
    (index: 2073, title: "Mass Invisibility", text: "Your units are invisible for the battle: attackers that do not see through illusions are at -1 to hit them."),
    (index: 2074, title: "Great Unsummoning", text: "Banishes every fantastic creature on both planes, yours too, unless it passes a resistance check at -2 against sorcery."),
    (index: 2075, title: "Spell Binding", text: "Takes an enemy wizard's overland enchantment and makes it yours, unless the enchantment resists."),
    (index: 2076, title: "Flying Fortress", text: "Makes your city fly. It cannot be reached by units that cannot fly, and the city still keeps its walls."),
    (index: 2077, title: "Sky Drake", text: "Summons Sky Drake onto the chosen square: melee 20, ranged 20, defence 10, resistance 14, 1 figure of 25 hit points, 4 moves. Abilities: Illusion Immunity, Magic Immunity, Flying, Lightning Breath."),
    (index: 2078, title: "Suppress Magic", text: "A standing dispel of strength 500 against every spell the other wizards cast on the map."),
    (index: 2079, title: "Time Stop", text: "Time stops for everyone but you. You pay no gold and eat no food while it lasts, only the spell's mana."),
    (index: 2080, title: "Warp Wood", text: "Warps the wooden weapons and bows of one enemy unit. Its ranged attacks cannot be used in this battle."),
    (index: 2081, title: "Disrupt", text: "Disrupts a wall of an enemy city on the battlefield, so the wall can be crossed."),
    (index: 2082, title: "Fire Bolt", text: "A bolt of fire strikes one enemy unit. Each extra mana adds a point of strength. Fire Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 2083, title: "Hell Hounds", text: "Summons Hell Hounds onto the chosen square: melee 3, ranged 3, defence 2, resistance 6, 4 figures of 4 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Fire Breath."),
    (index: 2084, title: "Corruption", text: "Corrupts the land on the chosen square. The square gives no food or production until it is cleansed."),
    (index: 2085, title: "Eldritch Weapon", text: "Makes the unit's attacks magical and the defender blocks with one point less defence, for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2086, title: "Wall of Fire", text: "Wraps your city in a wall of fire, which burns the units that attack it."),
    (index: 2087, title: "Shatter", text: "Shatters the attacks of one enemy unit: its melee and ranged attack are cut to 1."),
    (index: 2088, title: "Warp Creature", text: "Warps one enemy normal unit, if it fails a resistance check at -1. One of three harms is picked at random and lasts the battle: its melee and ranged attack are halved, its defence is halved, or its resistance falls to 0. A unit is warped only once. Fantastic creatures are not affected."),
    (index: 2089, title: "Fire Elemental", text: "Summons Fire Elemental to fight for you in the battle: melee 12, defence 4, resistance 6, 1 figure of 10 hit points, 1 move. Abilities: Fire Immunity, Stoning Immunity, Poison Immunity."),
    (index: 2090, title: "Lightning Bolt", text: "A bolt of lightning that halves the defence strikes one enemy unit. Each extra mana adds a point of strength. Magic Immunity protects against it."),
    (index: 2091, title: "Fire Giant", text: "Summons Fire Giant onto the chosen square: melee 10, ranged 10, defence 5, resistance 7, 1 figure of 15 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Fire Immunity, Wall Crusher, Mountaineer, Rock Throwing."),
    (index: 2092, title: "Chaos Channels", text: "Gives one of your normal units a gift of chaos for good, overland or in a battle: demon skin (+3 defence), demon wings (flight, at least 2 moves) or a fiery breath (strength 2, for a unit with no ranged attack). The unit becomes a creature of chaos and cannot be channelled again. Undead and fantastic creatures cannot take it."),
    (index: 2093, title: "Flame Blade", text: "Adds +2 to a unit's melee and ranged attack, and makes its attacks magical, for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2094, title: "Gargoyles", text: "Summons Gargoyles onto the chosen square: melee 4, defence 8, resistance 7, 4 figures of 4 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Stoning Immunity, Poison Immunity."),
    (index: 2095, title: "Fireball", text: "A ball of fire bursts on one enemy unit and hurts the figures round it. Each three extra mana add a point of strength. Fire Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 2096, title: "Doom Bat", text: "Summons Doom Bat onto the chosen square: melee 10, defence 5, resistance 9, 1 figure of 20 hit points, 4 moves. Abilities: Flying, Immolation."),
    (index: 2097, title: "Raise Volcano", text: "Raises a volcano on the chosen square of land. It produces gold and production for you, until it is gone."),
    (index: 2098, title: "Immolation", text: "Wraps a unit in flames that burn every attacker who strikes it in melee, for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2099, title: "Chimeras", text: "Summons Chimera onto the chosen square: melee 7, ranged 4, defence 5, resistance 8, 4 figures of 8 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Flying, Fire Breath."),
    (index: 2100, title: "Warp Lightning", text: "A chain of lightning bolts, each one die weaker, strikes one enemy unit and halves its defence. Magic Immunity protects against it."),
    (index: 2101, title: "Metal Fires", text: "Your normal units, except those with Flame Blade, get +1 melee and +1 ranged attack and magical weapons."),
    (index: 2102, title: "Chaos Spawn", text: "Summons Chaos Spawn onto the chosen square: melee 1, ranged 4, defence 6, resistance 10, 1 figure of 15 hit points, 1 move. Abilities: Flying, Cause Fear, Poison Touch, Multiple Gaze."),
    (index: 2103, title: "Doom Bolt", text: "A bolt of doom, strength 10, strikes one enemy unit and ignores its defence. Magic Immunity protects against it."),
    (index: 2104, title: "Magic Vortex", text: "Raises a vortex of magic on the battlefield, which moves each round and hurts every unit it touches."),
    (index: 2105, title: "Efreet", text: "Summons Efreet onto the chosen square: melee 9, ranged 9, defence 7, resistance 10, 1 figure of 12 hit points, 3 moves. Abilities: Fire Immunity, Flying, Spell Caster, Fireball."),
    (index: 2106, title: "Fire Storm", text: "A storm of fire strikes every unit on the chosen square. Fire Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 2107, title: "Warp Reality", text: "Every unit but the creatures of chaos fights at -2 to hit, both sides."),
    (index: 2108, title: "Flame Strike", text: "Fire strikes every enemy unit on the battlefield at strength 15. Fire Immunity and Magic Immunity protect against it."),
    (index: 2109, title: "Chaos Rift", text: "A rift of chaos over an enemy city. Each turn every unit in it takes five strength-8 lightning bolts that pierce armour, and a building that nothing needs falls with a 5% chance."),
    (index: 2110, title: "Hydra", text: "Summons Hydra onto the chosen square: melee 6, ranged 5, defence 4, resistance 11, 9 figures of 10 hit points, 1 move. Abilities: Regeneration, Fire Breath."),
    (index: 2111, title: "Disintegrate", text: "Destroys one unit whose resistance is under 10. A unit with more is not harmed."),
    (index: 2112, title: "Meteor Storm", text: "A strength-4 fire attack on every unit outside a city, yours too. Each building of the other wizards' cities has a 1% chance to be destroyed. Your own cities are safe."),
    (index: 2113, title: "Great Wasting", text: "Each turn three to six squares of land are corrupted, which brings unrest to the cities round them. Corruption does not harm you."),
    (index: 2114, title: "Call Chaos", text: "Chaos strikes every enemy unit with one of eight outcomes picked at random for each: nothing, five points of healing (not for creatures of death), Chaos Channels, Warp Creature, a strength-15 Fire Bolt, Warp Lightning, a Doom Bolt or Disintegrate. Chaos Channels and Warp Creature are skipped on a unit that cannot take them."),
    (index: 2115, title: "Chaos Surge", text: "Your units of the chaos realm fight with +2 melee and +2 ranged attack, on the map and in battles."),
    (index: 2116, title: "Doom Mastery", text: "Every unit you train from now on is mutated by chaos."),
    (index: 2117, title: "Great Drake", text: "Summons Great Drake onto the chosen square: melee 30, ranged 30, defence 10, resistance 12, 1 figure of 30 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Flying, Fire Breath."),
    (index: 2118, title: "Call the Void", text: "Opens a void over an enemy city. Each building has a 50% chance to fall, every unit there takes 10 damage, each citizen but the first has an even chance to die, and the land round is corrupted."),
    (index: 2119, title: "Armageddon", text: "Each turn three to six squares are scorched and volcanoes rise, each of which gives you a point of power. The cities of the other wizards have two more rebels."),
    (index: 2120, title: "Bless", text: "Gives a unit +3 defence and resistance against the attacks of death and chaos for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2121, title: "Star Fires", text: "A bolt of holy fire strikes one enemy creature of chaos or death. Other units are not harmed."),
    (index: 2122, title: "Endurance", text: "Adds one move to a unit for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2123, title: "Holy Weapon", text: "Makes a unit's attacks magical and adds +1 to its chance to hit, for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2124, title: "Healing", text: "Heals a unit of up to five hit points."),
    (index: 2125, title: "Holy Armor", text: "Adds +2 to a unit's defence for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2126, title: "Just Cause", text: "Your people believe in you: one rebel is pacified in each of your cities, and your fame is 10 higher while the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2127, title: "True Light", text: "Creatures of life gain 1 melee, ranged attack, defence and resistance, and creatures of death lose 1 of each. True Light and Darkness cancel each other."),
    (index: 2128, title: "Guardian Spirit", text: "Summons Guardian Spirit onto the chosen square: melee 10, defence 4, resistance 10, 1 figure of 10 hit points, 1 move. Abilities: Resist All, Meld, Non-Corporeal."),
    (index: 2129, title: "Heroism", text: "Raises a unit to the Elite level of experience for as long as the spell is kept up. It ends once the unit has reached that level by itself."),
    (index: 2130, title: "True Sight", text: "Gives a unit Illusion Immunity: it sees through illusions and the invisible."),
    (index: 2131, title: "Plane Shift", text: "Shifts a unit to the other plane at once, wherever it stands."),
    (index: 2132, title: "Resurrection", text: "Brings a dead hero back to life in your wizard's fortress."),
    (index: 2133, title: "Dispel Evil", text: "Destroys one creature of chaos or death unless it passes a resistance check at -4; the undead resist at -9. Other units are not harmed."),
    (index: 2134, title: "Planar Seal", text: "Seals the planes: no unit of any wizard can shift planes while the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2135, title: "Unicorns", text: "Summons Unicorns onto the chosen square: melee 5, defence 3, resistance 7, 4 figures of 6 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Poison Immunity, Resist All, Teleport."),
    (index: 2136, title: "Raise Dead", text: "Raises a dead unit of the battle and brings it back to life, though hurt."),
    (index: 2137, title: "Planar Travel", text: "Gives a unit the Planar Travel ability for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2138, title: "Heavenly Light", text: "Fills the city with holy light: one rebel less, and an Eternal Night does not darken the battles fought there."),
    (index: 2139, title: "Prayer", text: "Your units fight with +1 to hit, +1 to block and +1 resistance for the battle."),
    (index: 2140, title: "Lionheart", text: "Gives a unit +3 melee, +3 ranged attack, +3 resistance and +3 hit points while the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2141, title: "Incarnation", text: "Calls Torin the Chosen to your service. If he has fallen, he returns with the experience he had."),
    (index: 2142, title: "Invulnerability", text: "Gives a unit Weapon Immunity for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2143, title: "Righteousness", text: "Gives a unit immunity to the attacks of chaos and death magic for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2144, title: "Prosperity", text: "Doubles the gold the city makes."),
    (index: 2145, title: "Altar of Battle", text: "Units you train in the city start with at least 120 experience."),
    (index: 2146, title: "Angel", text: "Summons Angel onto the chosen square: melee 13, defence 7, resistance 8, 1 figure of 15 hit points, 3 moves. Abilities: Illusion Immunity, Flying, Holy Bonus, Dispel Evil."),
    (index: 2147, title: "Stream of Life", text: "Doubles the growth of the city. There are no rebels in it, and the units there heal completely each turn."),
    (index: 2148, title: "Mass Healing", text: "Heals every unit of yours on the battlefield of up to five hit points, except the creatures of death."),
    (index: 2149, title: "Holy Word", text: "Each figure of each enemy fantastic creature dies unless it passes a resistance check; the undead resist at an extra -5."),
    (index: 2150, title: "High Prayer", text: "Your units fight with +1 to hit, +1 to block, +3 resistance, +2 melee and +2 defence for the battle. It replaces Prayer."),
    (index: 2151, title: "Inspirations", text: "Doubles the production of the city."),
    (index: 2152, title: "Astral Gate", text: "Makes the city an Astral Gate: a stack in it can shift to the other plane there, as at a tower of power."),
    (index: 2153, title: "Holy Arms", text: "Every normal unit you own, the undead excepted, fights with magical weapons and +1 to hit, in melee and at range."),
    (index: 2154, title: "Consecration", text: "Consecrates the city. Every corrupted square in its area is cleaned each turn, unrest falls by two, and no spell of death or chaos can be cast on the city or on the units in it."),
    (index: 2155, title: "Life Force", text: "A standing dispel of strength 500 against every death spell the other wizards cast on the map."),
    (index: 2156, title: "Tranquility", text: "A standing dispel of strength 500 against every chaos spell the other wizards cast on the map."),
    (index: 2157, title: "Crusade", text: "Raises the experience level of all your units by one, except fantastic creatures and the undead. Heroes count."),
    (index: 2158, title: "Arch Angel", text: "Summons Arch Angel onto the chosen square: melee 15, defence 10, resistance 12, 1 figure of 18 hit points, 4 moves. Abilities: Illusion Immunity, Flying, Major Spell Caster, Holy Bonus."),
    (index: 2159, title: "Charm of Life", text: "Each of your units has a quarter more hit points, at least one more, while the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2160, title: "Skeletons", text: "Summons Skeletons onto the chosen square: melee 3, defence 4, resistance 5, 6 figures of 1 hit point, 1 move. Abilities: Missile Immunity, Illusion Immunity, Cold Immunity, Death Immunity, Poison Immunity."),
    (index: 2161, title: "Weakness", text: "Weakens one enemy unit: its melee and ranged attack fall by 2 unless it passes a resistance check at -2."),
    (index: 2162, title: "Dark Rituals", text: "Dark rites in the city: the power of its religious buildings is doubled, but the city grows 25% slower and has one more rebel."),
    (index: 2163, title: "Cloak of Fear", text: "Gives a unit the Cause Fear ability for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2164, title: "Black Sleep", text: "Puts one enemy unit to sleep. It cannot move, attack or fly until the spell is dispelled."),
    (index: 2165, title: "Ghouls", text: "Summons Ghouls onto the chosen square: melee 4, defence 3, resistance 6, 4 figures of 3 hit points, 1 move. Abilities: Illusion Immunity, Cold Immunity, Death Immunity, Poison Immunity, Create Undead, Poison Touch."),
    (index: 2166, title: "Life Drain", text: "Drains the life of one enemy unit. A roll that beats its resistance against death costs it that many hit points, and each 5 mana put in beyond the cost makes it one harder to resist. Creatures of death and units with Death Immunity are not affected. A wizard who casts it gains 3 mana for each point drained; a hero or creature that casts it heals by the points."),
    (index: 2167, title: "Terror", text: "At the start of each of their turns each of your enemies must pass a resistance check against death, or it loses its turn (it can still strike back)."),
    (index: 2168, title: "Darkness", text: "Creatures of death gain 1 melee, ranged attack, defence and resistance, and creatures of life lose 1 of each. True Light and Darkness cancel each other."),
    (index: 2169, title: "Mana Leak", text: "At the start of each turn the enemy wizard loses 5 mana, and each enemy unit with spell shots loses one."),
    (index: 2170, title: "Drain Power", text: "Drains 10 to 200 mana from an enemy wizard, never more than the wizard has."),
    (index: 2171, title: "Possession", text: "Takes control of one enemy unit for the rest of the battle unless it resists."),
    (index: 2172, title: "Lycanthropy", text: "Turns a unit into a werewolf: it becomes a creature of death and gains the strength of the wolf."),
    (index: 2173, title: "Black Prayer", text: "Your enemies fight with -1 melee, ranged attack and defence and -2 resistance for the battle."),
    (index: 2174, title: "Black Channels", text: "Channels dark power into a unit: it gains +2 melee, +1 ranged attack, +1 defence, +1 resistance and +1 hit point, and becomes undead."),
    (index: 2175, title: "Night Stalker", text: "Summons Night Stalker onto the chosen square: melee 7, ranged 1, defence 3, resistance 8, 1 figure of 10 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Illusion Immunity, Cold Immunity, Death Immunity, Poison Immunity, Invisibility, Death Gaze."),
    (index: 2176, title: "Subversion", text: "Turns the other wizards against the target: their relations with it fall by 25, and every peace with it ends."),
    (index: 2177, title: "Wall of Darkness", text: "Wraps your city in darkness. Enemy units that attack it fight at a disadvantage."),
    (index: 2178, title: "Berserk", text: "A unit's melee attack is doubled, but its defence drops to 0, for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2179, title: "Shadow Demons", text: "Summons Shadow Demons onto the chosen square: melee 5, ranged 4, defence 4, resistance 8, 4 figures of 5 hit points, 1 move. Abilities: Illusion Immunity, Cold Immunity, Death Immunity, Poison Immunity, Weapon Immunity, Flying, Planar Travel, Non-Corporeal, Regeneration, Death Bolt."),
    (index: 2180, title: "Wraith Form", text: "A unit becomes Non-Corporeal and gains Weapon Immunity for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2181, title: "Wrack", text: "At the start of each turn each figure of each enemy unit without death immunity must pass a resistance check against death, or the unit loses a hit point."),
    (index: 2182, title: "Evil Presence", text: "An evil presence over an enemy city destroys the mana of its shrines, temples, parthenons and cathedrals. It does nothing to a city whose owner can use death magic, and cannot be cast on one."),
    (index: 2183, title: "Wraiths", text: "Summons Wraiths onto the chosen square: melee 7, defence 6, resistance 8, 4 figures of 8 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Illusion Immunity, Cold Immunity, Death Immunity, Poison Immunity, Weapon Immunity, Flying, Non-Corporeal, Life Steal."),
    (index: 2184, title: "Cloud of Shadow", text: "Hides your city in shadow. Enemy units with ranged attacks have trouble striking its defenders."),
    (index: 2185, title: "Warp Node", text: "Warps a magic node an enemy owns: it drains five power from its owner each turn, and no one else can use it."),
    (index: 2186, title: "Black Wind", text: "A black wind sweeps the chosen square and hits every unit on it. For each figure there is a resistance check against death at -1, and each figure that fails loses a figure's worth of hit points. Units protected from death magic are not touched."),
    (index: 2187, title: "Zombie Mastery", text: "Every normal unit you kill in a battle you win rises as a zombie on your side."),
    (index: 2188, title: "Famine", text: "Famine in an enemy city: it makes half the food, and unrest grows."),
    (index: 2189, title: "Cursed Lands", text: "A curse on the lands round an enemy city: it makes half the production, and it has one more rebel."),
    (index: 2190, title: "Cruel Unminding", text: "Strips casting skill from an enemy wizard for good."),
    (index: 2191, title: "Word of Death", text: "Kills one unit unless it passes a resistance check at -5 against death. Death Immunity protects against it."),
    (index: 2192, title: "Death Knights", text: "Summons Death Knights onto the chosen square: melee 9, defence 8, resistance 10, 4 figures of 8 hit points, 3 moves. Abilities: Illusion Immunity, Cold Immunity, Death Immunity, Poison Immunity, Weapon Immunity, Flying, Armour Piercing, First Strike, Life Steal."),
    (index: 2193, title: "Death Spell", text: "Each figure of each enemy unit dies unless it passes a resistance check at -2 against death. Death Immunity protects against it."),
    (index: 2194, title: "Animate Dead", text: "Raises a dead unit of the battle as an undead creature on your side."),
    (index: 2195, title: "Pestilence", text: "A plague in an enemy city: two more rebels, and each turn every citizen but the last has a 10% chance to die."),
    (index: 2196, title: "Eternal Night", text: "Every battle is fought in Darkness, except at a city with Heavenly Light."),
    (index: 2197, title: "Evil Omens", text: "Life and nature spells cost 50% more mana, for every wizard."),
    (index: 2198, title: "Death Wish", text: "Every enemy normal unit must pass a resistance check against death, or it dies. Heroes are not normal units."),
    (index: 2199, title: "Demon Lord", text: "Summons Demon Lord onto the chosen square: melee 20, ranged 10, defence 10, resistance 12, 1 figure of 20 hit points, 2 moves. Abilities: Illusion Immunity, Cold Immunity, Death Immunity, Poison Immunity, Weapon Immunity, Flying, Creature Summoning, Cause Fear, Life Steal, Death Bolt."),
    (index: 2200, title: "Magic Spirit", text: "Summons Magic Spirit onto the chosen square: melee 5, defence 4, resistance 8, 1 figure of 10 hit points, 1 move. Abilities: Meld, Non-Corporeal."),
    (index: 2201, title: "Dispel Magic", text: "Tries to remove the enchantments other wizards have put on a unit or on the battlefield. The more mana you put in, the stronger the dispel."),
    (index: 2202, title: "Summoning Circle", text: "Moves your wizard's summoning circle to the chosen city, where your summoned creatures appear."),
    (index: 2203, title: "Disenchant Area", text: "Removes enchantments of other wizards from a square of the map and everything on it, with a strength of 50."),
    (index: 2204, title: "Recall Hero", text: "Teleports one of your heroes from the battle to your wizard's fortress or summoning circle."),
    (index: 2205, title: "Detect Magic", text: "Shows you the spell each other wizard is casting."),
    (index: 2206, title: "Enchant Item", text: "Lets you craft a magic item with a power of your choice. The more powers, the more mana it costs."),
    (index: 2207, title: "Summon Hero", text: "Summons a random hero to your service. The hero joins you in the fortress or the summoning circle."),
    (index: 2208, title: "Awareness", text: "Shows you every city of the world, for as long as the spell is kept up."),
    (index: 2209, title: "Disjunction", text: "Destroys one overland enchantment of any wizard, for good, unless it resists."),
    (index: 2210, title: "Create Artifact", text: "Lets you craft a magic artifact with the powers of your choice. The more powers, the more mana it costs."),
    (index: 2211, title: "Summon Champion", text: "Summons a champion, a hero stronger than the usual ones, to your service."),
    (index: 2212, title: "Spell of Mastery", text: "The greatest of spells. When it has been cast through, you win the game. Every other wizard turns against you while you cast it."),
    (index: 2213, title: "Spell of Return", text: "Returns a banished wizard to the chosen city of the wizard's, where a new fortress rises."),
    (index: 230, title: "Reduced map", text: "The whole plane in miniature. Click it to move the main view there. The white box is the part of the map the main view shows."),
    (index: 279, title: "Barbarian townsfolk", text: "Barbarian cities grow fast (+20 people a turn). They cannot build an Animists Guild, a University or a Cathedral."),
    (index: 280, title: "Beastmen townsfolk", text: "Beastmen cities make half a mana for each citizen. They cannot build a Fantastic Stable or a Ship Yard."),
    (index: 281, title: "Dark elf townsfolk", text: "Dark elf cities grow very slowly (-20 people a turn) and make one mana for each citizen. They cannot build a Maritime Guild or a Cathedral."),
    (index: 282, title: "Draconian townsfolk", text: "Draconian cities grow slowly (-10 people a turn) and make half a mana for each citizen. They cannot build a Fantastic Stable, a Maritime Guild or a Mechanicians Guild."),
    (index: 283, title: "Dwarf townsfolk", text: "Dwarves double the bonus of the mines around their city, and their workers make 3 production each instead of 2. Their cities grow very slowly (-20 people a turn). They cannot build Stables, a Ship Yard, a University or a Parthenon."),
    (index: 284, title: "Gnoll townsfolk", text: "Gnoll cities grow slowly (-10 people a turn). They cannot build an Armorers Guild, an Animists Guild, a Maritime Guild, a Sages Guild or a Parthenon."),
    (index: 285, title: "Halfling townsfolk", text: "Halfling farmers grow 3 food each instead of 2. Halflings cannot build an Armorers Guild, Stables, a Ship Yard or a University."),
    (index: 286, title: "High elf townsfolk", text: "High elf cities grow very slowly (-20 people a turn) and make half a mana for each citizen. They cannot build a Maritime Guild or a Parthenon."),
    (index: 287, title: "High men townsfolk", text: "High men cannot build a Fantastic Stable. They have no other limits."),
    (index: 288, title: "Klackon townsfolk", text: "Klackon cities grow slowly (-10 people a turn), and their workers make 3 production each instead of 2. They cannot build a Sages Guild, a Ship Yard or a Temple. If your own race is Klackon, their cities have 2 less unrest."),
    (index: 289, title: "Lizardmen townsfolk", text: "Lizardmen cities grow quickly (+10 people a turn). They cannot build a War College, an Animists Guild, a Ship Wrights Guild, a Sawmill, a Sages Guild, a Parthenon or a Miners Guild."),
    (index: 290, title: "Nomad townsfolk", text: "Nomad cities add 50% to their trade, counted like a road bonus, and grow slowly (-10 people a turn). They cannot build a Maritime Guild or a Wizards Guild."),
    (index: 291, title: "Orc townsfolk", text: "Orcs grow at the normal rate and can build every building."),
    (index: 292, title: "Troll townsfolk", text: "Troll cities grow very slowly (-20 people a turn). They cannot build a Fantastic Stable, a Ship Yard, a Sages Guild or a Miners Guild."),
    (index: 368, title: "Alchemy gold", text: "The gold in the exchange. When you turn gold into mana, it is the gold you give. When you turn mana into gold, it is the gold you get."),
    (index: 369, title: "Alchemy ratio", text: "Slide it to change how much gold and mana are exchanged."),
    (index: 370, title: "Alchemy mana", text: "The mana in the exchange. When you turn mana into gold, it is the mana you give. When you turn gold into mana, it is the mana you get."),
    (index: 371, title: "Cancel", text: "Closes the exchange and changes nothing."),
    (index: 372, title: "Direction", text: "Switches between turning gold into mana and mana into gold."),
    (index: 373, title: "OK", text: "Makes the exchange. Without the Alchemy retort you lose half in the exchange."),
    (index: 376, title: "Cancel", text: "Leaves the production screen and changes nothing."),
    (index: 377, title: "OK", text: "Leaves the production screen and makes the city build what you selected."),
    (index: 378, title: "Description", text: "What the selected building does for the city, or the unit's strength and abilities."),
    (index: 379, title: "Allows", text: "Some buildings must stand before others, or before certain units, can be built. This lists what the selected building makes possible."),
    (index: 380, title: "Upkeep", text: "The gold the city pays each turn to keep the building."),
    (index: 381, title: "Cost", text: "The production the building or unit takes to finish. A unit costs less when the city holds coal and iron mines; the base cost is shown in brackets."),
    (index: 503, title: "Units", text: "The units standing on this square."),
    (index: 508, title: "Cancel", text: "Gives up the cast. The spell is lost, and so is the mana already paid for it."),
    (index: 509, title: "Casting", text: "The kind of spell you are casting and its name."),
    (index: 510, title: "Road building", text: "Click the map to choose where the engineers build the road. A blue line is a path they can build; a red line is a path they cannot. The number of turns the road will take is shown."),
    (index: 511, title: "OK", text: "The engineers start building the road."),
    (index: 512, title: "Cancel", text: "Gives up the road. The engineers keep their orders."),
    (index: 513, title: "Surveyor", text: "Move the mouse over the land to read what it is and what it gives."),
    (index: 514, title: "Cancel", text: "Closes the Surveyor."),
    (index: 589, title: "Spell", text: "Opens the spell book to cast a spell in this battle."),
    (index: 590, title: "Wait", text: "Puts this unit aside and selects the next one. It comes back later in the round."),
    (index: 591, title: "Info", text: "Lists the enchantments of the wizards, the city and the node that affect this battle."),
    (index: 592, title: "Auto", text: "The computer fights the battle for both sides until it ends."),
    (index: 593, title: "Flee", text: "Retreats from the battle. Each fleeing unit has a 50% chance of being destroyed; a fleeing hero has 25%. On Intro and Easy the player whose turn it is loses no unit by fleeing, but units that are asleep, confused or held in a web are always lost."),
    (index: 594, title: "Done", text: "Ends this unit's turn."),
    (index: 595, title: "Skill", text: "Your casting skill: the most mana you can spend on spells in one battle."),
    (index: 626, title: "Damage", text: "How much damage the unit has taken."),
    (index: 636, title: "Save", text: "Saves the game in the selected slot."),
    (index: 637, title: "OK", text: "Goes back to the main screen."),
    (index: 639, title: "Saved games", text: "Click a slot to save the game there, or to load the game saved in it."),
    (index: 658, title: "Banner", text: "Pick the colour of your banner. It marks your units and the flags of your cities."),
    (index: 659, title: "Merlin", text: "Wizard of life and nature, with five books of each. A Sage Master: his research is 25% faster."),
    (index: 660, title: "Raven", text: "A native shaman of sorcery and nature, with six books of sorcery and five of nature."),
    (index: 661, title: "Sharee", text: "A voodoo priestess of death and chaos, with five books of each. A Conjurer: summoning spells cost her 25% less."),
    (index: 662, title: "Lo Pan", text: "An eastern mystic of sorcery and chaos, with four books of sorcery and five of chaos. A Channeler: he casts in battle as if the battle were at his fortress, and pays half the upkeep of his spells."),
    (index: 663, title: "Jafar", text: "A nomad sorcerer with ten books of sorcery. He has Alchemy: he exchanges gold and mana one for one, and every unit his cities build has a magic weapon."),
    (index: 664, title: "Oberic", text: "An elementalist of nature and chaos, with five books of each. He has Mana Focusing: the mana he gets from his power is 25% greater."),
    (index: 665, title: "Tauron", text: "A demonic force with ten books of chaos. He has Chaos Mastery: his chaos spells research faster and cost less, are harder to dispel, and chaos nodes give him twice the power."),
    (index: 666, title: "Sss'ra", text: "A draconian warlock of life and chaos, with four books of each. A Myrran: he starts on Myrror with a Myrror race."),
    (index: 667, title: "Rjak", text: "A warlock with nine books of death. He has Infernal Power: shrines, temples, parthenons and cathedrals give him 50% more power and calm."),
    (index: 668, title: "Freya", text: "An elvish sylph with ten books of nature. She has Nature Mastery: her nature spells research faster and cost less, are harder to dispel, and nature nodes give her twice the power."),
    (index: 669, title: "Horus", text: "A sorcerer of life and sorcery, with five books of each. An Archmage: his casting skill is 10 higher."),
    (index: 670, title: "Ariel", text: "A high priestess with ten books of life. Charismatic: she pays half for heroes, mercenaries and magic items, and her diplomacy gains double and its losses are halved."),
    (index: 671, title: "Tlaloc", text: "An Aztec priest of nature and death, with four books of nature and five of death. A Warlord: all his units have one level more, and may rise above Elite."),
    (index: 672, title: "Kali", text: "A witch of death and sorcery, with five books of each. An Artificer: magic items cost her half, and she begins with Enchant Item and Create Artifact."),
    (index: 674, title: "Portrait", text: "Pick the picture of your wizard."),
    (index: 693, title: "Alchemy", text: "Exchange gold and mana one for one, instead of losing half. Every unit built in your cities has a magic weapon."),
    (index: 694, title: "Warlord", text: "All your units have one level more, and may rise above Elite to Ultra Elite. Costs 2 picks."),
    (index: 695, title: "Channeler", text: "Cast in battle as if the battle were at your fortress, with no extra mana, and pay half the upkeep of your spells. Costs 2 picks."),
    (index: 696, title: "Archmage", text: "Casting skill 10 higher, and your spells are twice as hard to dispel. The mana you put into skill gives half as much again."),
    (index: 697, title: "Artificer", text: "Magic items cost half to make. You begin with Enchant Item and Create Artifact."),
    (index: 698, title: "Conjurer", text: "Summoning spells cost 25% less to research and to cast."),
    (index: 699, title: "Sage Master", text: "Your research is 25% faster in every realm."),
    (index: 700, title: "Myrran", text: "You start on Myrror with a Myrror race, and your fortress makes 5 more mana. Costs 3 picks."),
    (index: 701, title: "Divine Power", text: "Shrines, temples, parthenons and cathedrals give you 50% more power and calm. Costs 2 picks."),
    (index: 702, title: "Famous", text: "You start with 10 fame, and heroes, mercenaries and magic items are offered to you twice as often. Costs 2 picks."),
    (index: 703, title: "Runemaster", text: "Arcane spells research 25% faster and cost 25% less to cast."),
    (index: 704, title: "Charismatic", text: "Heroes, mercenaries and magic items cost you half. Good diplomatic actions toward you count double and bad ones half."),
    (index: 705, title: "Chaos Mastery", text: "Chaos spells research 15% faster and cost 15% less to cast, and are twice as hard to dispel. Chaos nodes give you twice the power."),
    (index: 706, title: "Nature Mastery", text: "Nature spells research 15% faster and cost 15% less to cast, and are twice as hard to dispel. Nature nodes give you twice the power."),
    (index: 707, title: "Sorcery Mastery", text: "Sorcery spells research 15% faster and cost 15% less to cast, and are twice as hard to dispel. Sorcery nodes give you twice the power."),
    (index: 708, title: "Infernal Power", text: "Shrines, temples, parthenons and cathedrals give you 50% more power and calm. Costs 2 picks."),
    (index: 709, title: "Mana Focusing", text: "The mana you get from your power is 25% greater."),
    (index: 710, title: "Node Mastery", text: "Nodes give you twice the power, and your spells cannot be dispelled by a node."),
    (index: 712, title: "OK", text: "Accepts the wizard as designed. Only works once all your picks are spent."),
    (index: 757, title: "Page back", text: "Turns to the previous page."),
    (index: 758, title: "Page forward", text: "Turns to the next page."),
    (index: 759, title: "Cancel", text: "Gives up the spell. The mana already paid for it is lost."),
    (index: 760, title: "Extra mana cost", text: "The extra mana it costs to Spell Blast the wizard you have selected."),
    (index: 763, title: "Tax rate", text: "Sets the tax. Each citizen pays the gold shown every turn, and the percentage shown is the share of the city that becomes unrest. A city's income also depends on a shore, a river, roads, and on its Marketplace, Bank and Merchants Guild."),
    (index: 764, title: "Advisors", text: "Pick an advisor to report on your progress and your surroundings."),
    (index: 777, title: "Death spells", text: "Death raises the dead and calls on the dark. Its enchantments bring disease and misfortune on the enemy."),
    (index: 778, title: "Chaos spells", text: "Chaos corrupts and destroys, calling on the elemental forces of change."),
    (index: 779, title: "Life spells", text: "Life heals, protects and inspires, and opens the way between planes. It stands against Death, and resists Chaos."),
    (index: 780, title: "Nature spells", text: "Nature commands earth and water, and the growth of the land."),
    (index: 781, title: "Sorcery spells", text: "Sorcery rules air and illusion, and holds the spells that resist and control other wizards' magic."),
    (index: 799, title: "Spells", text: "1 point for each spell you know."),
    (index: 800, title: "Townsfolk", text: "Half a point for each citizen in your cities."),
    (index: 801, title: "Banished wizards", text: "50 points for each wizard you defeated."),
    (index: 802, title: "Fame", text: "2 points for each point of fame."),
    (index: 803, title: "Year", text: "2000 less 2 points for each turn played. You only get these points while your fortress stands and nobody has cast the Spell of Mastery before you; late in the game they can be negative."),
    (index: 804, title: "Spell of Mastery", text: "250 points for casting the Spell of Mastery."),
    (index: 805, title: "Final score", text: "The sum of all the points, scaled by the difficulty: Intro halves it, Easy takes three quarters, Normal leaves it, Hard doubles it and Impossible triples it."),
    (index: 807, title: "Play intro", text: "Whether the opening movie plays when the game starts. It plays only if its pictures were extracted."),
    (index: 808, title: "Left click moves units", text: "On: a left click on the map moves the selected units there, and a right click selects what is under the pointer. Off: the buttons swap roles."),
    (index: 809, title: "Dim behind boxes", text: "Whether the screen under a question or a notice is dimmed while the box is open."),
    // Buildings: each row of buildings.ron names its topic with `help` (2300 + the building's number).
    (index: 2303, title: "Barracks", text: "Lets the city train its regular soldiers."),
    (index: 2304, title: "Armory", text: "Lets the city build halberdiers (for most races) and halfling slingers. Needs Smithy and Barracks."),
    (index: 2305, title: "Fighters Guild", text: "New units start with at least 20 experience. Teaches basic fighting skills. Needs Armory."),
    (index: 2306, title: "Armorers Guild", text: "Skilled armorers outfit the troops. Needs Fighters Guild."),
    (index: 2307, title: "War College", text: "New units start with at least 60 experience. Teaches advanced tactics. Needs University and Armorers Guild."),
    (index: 2308, title: "Smithy", text: "A forge for weapons and tools. Opens the way to better military and trade buildings."),
    (index: 2309, title: "Stables", text: "Raises and trains horses, so the city can field mounted troops. Needs Smithy."),
    (index: 2310, title: "Animists Guild", text: "+1 food from each farmer, -1 unrest, +3 mana. Followers of nature tend the city. Needs Temple and Stables."),
    (index: 2311, title: "Fantastic Stable", text: "Keeps fantastic beasts, so the city can build the strongest mounts and monsters. Needs Armorers Guild and Animists Guild."),
    (index: 2312, title: "Ship Wrights Guild", text: "Builds simple ships for a city on the coast."),
    (index: 2313, title: "Ship Yard", text: "A larger dock for sturdier warships and trading vessels. Needs Sawmill and Ship Wrights Guild."),
    (index: 2314, title: "Maritime Guild", text: "The master of sea power: the biggest ships and the best crews. Needs Armory and Ship Yard."),
    (index: 2315, title: "Sawmill", text: "+25% production. Turns timber into building material."),
    (index: 2316, title: "Library", text: "+2 research. Books and scholars gather here. Needs Builders Hall."),
    (index: 2317, title: "Sages Guild", text: "+3 research. Learned sages gather here. Needs Library."),
    (index: 2318, title: "Oracle", text: "-2 unrest, sees 9 squares around. Foretells the future. Needs Parthenon and University."),
    (index: 2319, title: "Alchemists Guild", text: "Brews potions and refines metal: units built in the city get magic weapons, or mithril or adamantium when the city works such an ore. Needs Sages Guild."),
    (index: 2320, title: "University", text: "+5 research. A seat of learning. Needs Sages Guild."),
    (index: 2321, title: "Wizards Guild", text: "+8 research, +3 mana. Mages gather here to study. Needs Alchemists Guild and University."),
    (index: 2322, title: "Shrine", text: "+1 mana, -1 unrest. A place of worship. Needs Builders Hall."),
    (index: 2323, title: "Temple", text: "+2 mana, -1 unrest. A larger house of worship. Needs Shrine."),
    (index: 2324, title: "Parthenon", text: "+3 mana, -1 unrest. A grand monument to the divine. Needs Temple."),
    (index: 2325, title: "Cathedral", text: "+4 mana, -1 unrest. The greatest house of worship. Needs Parthenon."),
    (index: 2326, title: "Marketplace", text: "+50% gold. Traders gather here. Needs Smithy."),
    (index: 2327, title: "Bank", text: "+50% gold. Lends and stores money. Needs Marketplace and University."),
    (index: 2328, title: "Merchants Guild", text: "+100% gold. A guild of great traders. Needs Ship Yard and Bank."),
    (index: 2329, title: "Granary", text: "+2 food, +20 people growth each turn. Stores grain against bad times. Needs Builders Hall."),
    (index: 2330, title: "Farmers Market", text: "+3 food, +30 people growth each turn. Farmers sell their crops directly. Needs Granary and Marketplace."),
    (index: 2331, title: "Foresters Guild", text: "+2 food, +25% production. Foresters tend the woods. Needs Sawmill."),
    (index: 2332, title: "Builders Hall", text: "The base of all city works. Many other buildings need it first."),
    (index: 2333, title: "Mechanicians Guild", text: "+50% production. Engineers build machines. Needs Miners Guild and University."),
    (index: 2334, title: "Miners Guild", text: "+50% production. Miners work the nearby hills. Needs Builders Hall."),
    (index: 2335, title: "City Walls", text: "Sees 7 squares around. In battle a wall rings the city: attackers can pass it only through the gate. Needs Builders Hall."),
]
